2,2,2,2,9,9,9,9,9],[4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,2,2,2,2,9,9,9,9,9],[4,4,4,9,9,2,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,2,2,2,2,9,9,9,9,9],[4,4,4,4,8,3,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,2,2,2,2,9,9,9,9,9],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,1,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,4]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"The grid is cut into four quadrants by a full row and a full column of colour 1.\n\n**The template.** One quadrant holds a multicolour figure: a square block of colour 2 with coloured pieces attached around it.\n- Pair 1: an 8 block above the 2 block and a 3 block to its right.\n- Pair 2: a 9 bar on the left, 1s on the right, and a 3 and an 8 above.\n\n**The targets.** Each of the other quadrants holds lone squares of colour 2. These come in different sizes: 1×1, 2×2, 3×3 and 4×4.\n\n**What the output does.** Around every lone 2-square, the template's attachments are redrawn. Three things change:\n\n1. **Scale.** The template is resized by the ratio (target square size) / (template 2-block size).\n   - Pair 1: the template block is 2×2. A 3×3 target gets 3×3 attachments, and the 1×1 target gets single cells.\n   - Pair 2: the 4×4 target gets every template piece doubled.\n2. **Mirror.** The template is reflected according to where the target quadrant sits relative to the template quadrant.\n   - A quadrant in the other column gets a left-right flip. In pair 1, the 3 moves from the right side to the left side.\n   - A quadrant in the other row gets an up-down flip. The 8 moves from above to below.\n   - The diagonal quadrant gets both flips.\n3. **Alignment.** The scaled, mirrored template is placed so that its 2-block lands exactly on the target square. Only the non-background cells are painted, and anything that falls outside the grid is clipped. This matters in pair 2, where the bottom-left 3 piece reaches the bottom border.\n\n**How the code does it.**\n- The template quadrant is the one whose content uses colours other than background and 2.\n- To scale, each target pixel samples the template pixel at floor(offset · s0 / s), where s0 is the template block size and s the target size. This one formula covers both enlarging and shrinking, such as 2×2 → 1×1 in pair 1.\n- Then the patch is flipped and pasted.\n\n**On the test.**\n- The template (top-left) is a 2×2 block of 2 with: 8 and 3 blocks above it, a 9 bar of width 4 to its left, and a 1 block below it.\n- Top-right: a 3×3 square, so scale 1.5 with a left-right flip.\n- Bottom-left: a 1×1 square, so scale ½ with an up-down flip. The 9 bar becomes 1×2.\n- Bottom-right: a 4×4 square, so scale 2 with both flips.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    out = g.copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    dv = dividers(g)\n    rows = [r for r, _ in dv[\"rows\"]]\n    cols = [c for c, _ in dv[\"cols\"]]\n    pans = panels(g)\n    divcols = set(c for _, c in dv[\"rows\"]) | set(c for _, c in dv[\"cols\"])\n\n    def quad(y, x):\n        return (sum(1 for r in rows if y > r), sum(1 for c in cols if x > c))\n\n    # find template panel: contains colours other than bg and 2 (and divider colour)\n    tpl = None\n    for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in pans:\n        sub = g[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1]\n        cs = set(np.unique(sub)) - {bg, 2}\n        if cs:\n            tpl = (y0, x0, y1, x1)\n            break\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = tpl\n    sub = g[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1]\n    ys, xs = np.where(sub != bg)\n    P = sub[ys.min():ys.max() + 1, xs.min():xs.max() + 1]\n    two = np.argwhere(P == 2)\n    br, bc = two.min(0)\n    s0 = two[:, 0].max() - br + 1\n    tq = quad(y0, x0)\n\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        if o[\"colour\"] != 2:\n            continue\n        oy0, ox0, oy1, ox1 = o[\"box\"]\n        if quad(oy0, ox0) == tq:\n            continue\n        s = oy1 - oy0 + 1\n        H = P.shape[0] * s // s0\n        W = P.shape[1] * s // s0\n        Q = np.full((H, W), bg)\n        for i in range(H):\n            for j in range(W):\n                Q[i, j] = P[i * s0 // s, j * s0 // s]\n        r2, c2 = br * s // s0, bc * s // s0\n        q = quad(oy0, ox0)\n        if q[1] != tq[1]:\n            Q = Q[:, ::-1]\n            c2 = W - (c2 + s)\n        if q[0] != tq[0]:\n            Q = Q[::-1, :]\n            r2 = H - (r2 + s)\n        ty, tx = oy0 - r2, ox0 - c2\n        for i in range(H):\n            for j in range(W):\n                v = Q[i, j]\n                yy, xx = ty + i, tx + j\n                if v != bg and 0 <= yy < g.shape[0] and 0 <= xx < g.shape[1]:\n                    out[yy, xx] = v\n        emit(out, f\"Stamped template scaled to size {s} (mirrored for quadrant {q}) around the 2-square at {(oy0, ox0)}\")\n    emit(out, \"All lone 2-squares decorated with the scaled, mirrored template\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Mirror.** The template is reflected according to where the target quadrant sits relative to the template quadrant."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Alignment.** The scaled, mirrored template is placed so that its 2-block lands exactly on the target square."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamped template scaled to size 2 (mirrored for quadrant (0, 1)) around the 2-square at (5, 20)"}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Alignment.** The scaled, mirrored template is placed so that its 2-block lands exactly on the target square."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**The template.** One quadrant holds a multicolour figure: a square block of colour 2 with coloured pieces attached around it."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What the output does.** Around every lone 2-square, the template's attachments are redrawn."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Scale.** The template is resized by the ratio (target square size) / (template 2-block size)."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Only the non-background cells are painted, and anything that falls outside the grid is clipped."}],"scale":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Scale.** The template is resized by the ratio (target square size) / (template 2-block size)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Alignment.** The scaled, mirrored template is placed so that its 2-block lands exactly on the target square."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- To scale, each target pixel samples the template pixel at floor(offset · s0 / s), where s0 is the template block size and s the target size."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"e31055c9db5cd5a3d98de562a5de8d58a9c65f82c32160db26083c774434d943","task_sha256":"8513af74286df4cef299149f9265298aa199781693a3a44593bc0de8c0f388a7","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
